      "statement": "withBudget enforces --max-cost preventively around every call: a pre-check throws MaxCostExceededError before dispatching once cumulative spend crosses the cap, and a post-check throws immediately after the call that crosses it, with the message \"Cost $X exceeded limit of $Y (aborted after \\\"role\\\")\"; because a call's cost is only known after it completes, the leg that detects the overrun is always billed.",
